WEBVTT

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:27.050
Joe, hurry up! We'll be late!

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:27.950
Sure.

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:16.940
Rikiishi-kun, it's time.

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:45.470
Rikiishi-kun, you can't possibly fight in your condition!

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:49.890
I'll be fine, Miss.

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:54.010
Today's match is no more than a tryout for my fight with Yabuki.

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:57.390
It shouldn't be a problem.

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:11.590
I just don't get it.

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:15.690
Hey, old man, why do you think they got this Filipino to fight

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:17.970
in Rikiishi's first match as a bantamweight?

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:18.960
It doesn't make any sense.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:21.470
Because he has no other opponents.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:22.970
Opponents?

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:27.470
Rikiishi's feared for his outstandingly powerful punches, even for the featherweight division.

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:31.670
Now that he's dropped one weight class to bantamweight,

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:34.810
I can't blame all the other boxers for keeping their distance.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:43.450
I get it.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.610
So they had no choice but to bring in a foreigner

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:48.450
who doesn't know how powerful Rikiishi is.

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:53.000
This fight'll be a piece of cake for Rikiishi.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:11.870
Hey, take a look at that Filipino!

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:13.990
He's all covered with scars!

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:16.230
How can he be so calm?

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:19.550
That Leo is quite a tough fighter.

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:21.570
He may currently be just eighth in his division,

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:27.450
but as those scars show, he's a veteran with a ten-year career.

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:31.790
He may not be as fast as he used to,

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:35.540
but the killer punch he was known for in his glory days is still going strong.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:39.010
Oh. So this is gonna be a real slugfest.

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:40.270
Sounds like fun.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:46.610
Here comes Rikiishi!

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:48.180
Showing off by coming in fashionably late, is he?

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.230
We've been waiting for you, ladykiller! Rikiishi!

00:04:57.110 --> 00:04:59.000
Send him packing, Rikiishi!

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.400
You're so cool!

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:08.710
Rikiishi! We're all supporting your bantamweight transfer!

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:11.450
Because then we'll get to see you fight Joe the Brawler!

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:12.120
Yeah!

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:12.750
That's right!

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:17.250
Rikiishi, the fans all get the idea.

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:25.110
Yohko.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:34.770
<i>In the red corner, in eighth place in the Filipino Bantamweight Division,</i>

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:40.270
<i>weighing in at 117-and-a-half pounds, Pancho Leo!{apparently this is grammatically correct number usage}</i>

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:45.090
<i>In the blue corner, the Japanese bantamweight associated with Shiraki Gym,</i>

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:50.240
<i>weighing in at 118 pounds, Rikiishi Toru!</i>

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:52.750
118 pounds. Impressive.

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:54.870
He made it just under the bantamweight limit.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:58.910
Hey, Rikiishi! I'll be watching!

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:00.250
You better stick with it!

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:21.610
Rikiishi definitely feels like he's lost weight...

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:28.050
They say the face is the last part of the body where weight is lost.

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:30.550
And with his face that hollowed...

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:35.200
Seconds out!

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:16.090
N-Now, this is no joke!

00:07:16.090 --> 00:07:19.540
Can weight loss this drastic even be considered humane?{"weight loss this drastic" is different TL from "this drastic weight loss"}

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:25.090
Certainly not, if the gym's coaches and manager forced it upon him.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:29.550
But I've heard that in Rikiishi's case, this was of his own volition.

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:34.170
You mean so he could settle his grudge match with Yabuki Joe?

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:35.310
That's right.

00:07:35.310 --> 00:07:39.060
But that said, he should naturally be lacking in stamina

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:41.670
with such a gaunt frame.

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:46.730
So the problem is whether or not he can stand up against the veteran Leo's blows.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:55.530
This was his only choice.

00:07:55.530 --> 00:08:00.550
Because he made the irrational choice to go down to bantamweight with that frame and physique,

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:02.250
this was his only choice.

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:28.650
R-Rikiishi...

00:08:46.030 --> 00:08:48.450
Leo came out swinging as soon as the bell rang!

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:50.390
Rikiishi's backing up to observe Leo's...

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:09.400
Rikiishi...

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:15.750
What's wrong with you, Rikiishi?

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:17.700
Why the hell are you just standing there?

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:19.070
Punch! Punch back!

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:28.910
Leo's now switched to body blows!

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:31.500
Rikiishi's up against the ropes, simply defending!

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:36.740
Leo's not letting up for a second!

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:38.730
It's a right! Now a left! That was intense!

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:39.800
Rikiishi's in trouble here!

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.360
Stop! That's the bell!

00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:56.920
That's the bell, that's the bell!

00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:58.320
Didn't you hear it, dumbass?

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:00.320
That's the bell!

00:10:13.790 --> 00:10:15.250
What's wrong with him?

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:16.910
Is that really Rikiishi?

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:19.510
Has he lost too much weight for his own good?{supposed to be negative connotation}

00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:26.950
Even considering the toll Rikiishi's diet has taken on him, this is just hard to watch!

00:10:26.950 --> 00:10:31.700
In that first round, Rikiishi only managed to throw two uppercuts!

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:33.790
And they didn't even scratch Leo!

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:36.670
But compared to that, weren't Leo's attacks amazing?

00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:41.990
Yes. From jabs to straights to hooks, he had the variety you'd expect from a veteran!

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:47.350
Grandfather!

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:50.550
Rikiishi-kun can barely even stand, much less fight!

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:53.450
Even an amateur can tell that continuing the fight is too dangerous!

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:55.190
I'll have the second throw in the towel!

00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:57.500
If you admit you're an amateur, then shut up and watch!

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:03.470
Rikiishi-kun's a professional.

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:05.450
He knows that he can barely stand,

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:08.510
but he'd rather die than call the match.

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:11.520
We just have to let him go as far as he can.

00:11:35.350 --> 00:11:37.710
He did it! He got an uppercut in!

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:41.260
Get to a neutral corner!

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:44.260
<i>1!</i>

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:45.550
<i>2!</i>

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:46.770
<i>3!</i>

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:48.260
<i>4!</i>

00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:49.240
<i>5!{changed to An style}</i>

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:50.670
C-Count no thank you!

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:51.910
That was lucky punch!

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:53.230
I continue match!

00:12:00.670 --> 00:12:01.490
<i>Fight!</i>

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:06.650
Rikiishi! Keep it up!

00:12:06.650 --> 00:12:09.160
Knock out that scarred old fart!

00:12:19.030 --> 00:12:21.190
This was his only choice.

00:12:21.190 --> 00:12:26.890
Because he made the irrational choice to go down to bantamweight with that frame and physique,

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:28.710
this was his only choice.

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:31.640
Keep going, Rikiishi.

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:35.350
It may be irrational, it may be immature,

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:37.010
but this is our world.

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:42.570
This would be the inevitable result if we were ever to cross gloves.

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:46.490
Rikiishi, hang in there!

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:48.050
Hang in there!

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:23.400
R-Rikiishi!

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:40.530
You're not a sandbag!

00:13:40.530 --> 00:13:41.670
Why the hell are you letting him hit you?

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:43.930
Do something! Hit back!

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:45.170
Rikiishi!

00:14:02.090 --> 00:14:04.570
Rikiishi's throwing tremendous uppercuts with all his strength!

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:05.820
Leo can't fight back!

00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:09.650
Oh! Leo's right straight has connected with Rikiishi's face!

00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:11.110
Now a left! And another right!

00:14:13.190 --> 00:14:16.110
The uppercut is the greatest of all knockout punches,

00:14:16.110 --> 00:14:19.490
but because of the bigger swing, it's easier for the opponent to counter.

00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:20.330
But...

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:23.930
If he's still throwing them, even knowing that,

00:14:23.930 --> 00:14:25.310
there must be a reason behind it!

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:39.390
That son of a bitch is still laughing!

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:40.750
Go, Rikiishi!

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:43.650
Pound that shit-eating grin off his face!

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:44.900
Hey, Joe!

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:46.850
Go, go, go, go, go!

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:08.950
Shit!

00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:15.850
Rikiishi, what are you, stupid?

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:19.600
Leo's a veteran, yet you keep telegraphing those huge uppercuts like a fucking idiot!

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:23.610
You don't even have the goddamn stamina thanks to your weight loss!

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:27.750
I-I don't blame his rival Yabuki Joe for being angry.

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:31.670
After all, Rikiishi's done nothing in the first and second rounds

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:34.280
but throw uppercut after uppercut.

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:40.960
He probably doesn't realize that Leo could see those uppercuts from a mile away.

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:46.630
In fact, in cases of extreme stamina loss, the ability to think is dulled.

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:47.960
It really is awful.

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:55.600
Joe, don't make such a fuss.

00:15:57.130 --> 00:15:58.860
Then what am I supposed to do?

00:15:58.860 --> 00:16:02.750
How could Rikiishi fight such an unsightly fight?

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:03.610
How the hell?

00:16:04.870 --> 00:16:07.610
It's unsettling precisely because it's unsightly.

00:16:13.710 --> 00:16:15.970
What's that supposed to mean, huh?

00:16:24.990 --> 00:16:27.630
Well, let's just watch the match.

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:37.050
Once again, Rikiishi's throwing uppercuts and missing!

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:38.970
And Leo skillfully dodges those uppercuts!

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:40.960
And he's going for Rikiishi's flank!

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.890
You did it! Way to go, Rikiishi!

00:16:48.890 --> 00:16:50.400
He hit him!

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:52.900
He hit him with another uppercut!

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:00.990
That's it, Rikiishi! Don't let up!

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:02.870
Finish him off as soon as he gets up!

00:17:03.510 --> 00:17:04.850
Get to a neutral corner!

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:06.790
<i>1!</i>

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:08.170
<i>2!</i>

00:17:08.970 --> 00:17:10.450
<i>3!</i>

00:17:10.450 --> 00:17:11.890
<i>4!</i>

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:13.370
<i>5!</i>

00:17:13.370 --> 00:17:14.210
<i>6!</i>

00:17:14.830 --> 00:17:16.390
<i>7!</i>

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:17.720
<i>8!</i>

00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:19.370
<i>Fight!</i>

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:23.190
Now, Rikiishi! Get him!

00:17:23.190 --> 00:17:24.350
Go, go, go!

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:30.450
Rikiishi! Finish him off with your special triple-blow!

00:17:30.450 --> 00:17:31.360
Go!

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:43.330
Uppercuts again...

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:48.000
Why the hell are you just throwing uppercuts like a one-trick pony?

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:50.500
Have you forgotten all the other punches?

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:56.150
Rikiishi's in trouble again!

00:17:56.150 --> 00:17:58.130
He'd be down if it weren't for the ropes!

00:17:58.130 --> 00:17:59.640
Ah, this isn't good!

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.370
He's in a condition where he can't trust his stamina,

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:04.430
but he's just wasting it by throwing nothing but uppercuts!

00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:18.290
What's the matter with you?

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:21.830
Have you lost so much weight that you can't even throw a straight punch?

00:18:23.990 --> 00:18:25.710
You can't throw any more uppercuts, Rikiishi-kun!

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:27.290
He's already used to them!

00:18:37.370 --> 00:18:38.610
Now Rikiishi's throwing jabs!

00:18:38.610 --> 00:18:39.840
This is the first time this entire fight!

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:41.300
J-Jab...

00:19:11.550 --> 00:19:12.380
Doctor!

00:19:28.370 --> 00:19:30.890
He settled it so quickly.

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:34.400
I see. I get it now!

00:19:38.970 --> 00:19:40.890
He got his opponent's eyes used to uppercuts,

00:19:40.890 --> 00:19:42.790
then suddenly started attacking head-on!

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:46.690
Can't dodge that, can you?

00:19:48.270 --> 00:19:51.450
But for you, Rikiishi, that's a pretty juvenile strategy.

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:52.330
Let me make this clear...

00:19:54.410 --> 00:19:57.340
Those childish tricks won't mean a thing when you fight me!

00:20:02.150 --> 00:20:03.450
You idiot!

00:20:04.910 --> 00:20:06.350
Don't be so cocky!

00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:08.010
You haven't even figured out the meaning of his strategy!

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:11.020
The meaning of his strategy?

00:20:11.570 --> 00:20:15.890
Joe, you've only ever been good with one strategy, and that's hanging your arms limp at your side.

00:20:15.890 --> 00:20:20.510
Don't you see that his uppercut strategy can demolish your No Guard strategy?

00:20:21.980 --> 00:20:24.770
Wh-What?

00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:27.970
You can only use your special Cross Counter

00:20:27.970 --> 00:20:30.750
if the opponent throws a straight punch!

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:33.960
But you can't do a thing against the uppercut!

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:38.230
Not only does the opponent's center of gravity not go forward,

00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:40.670
it almost bends backwards!

00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:44.970
So you can't even use a regular counter, much less the Cross Counter!

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:48.350
Congratulations, Rikiishi-kun.

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:49.750
You did well, Rikiishi-kun.

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:51.980
You fought well for your condition.

00:20:52.950 --> 00:20:55.980
Thank you very much.

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:04.730
Even after suffering from his weight loss, and facing such a veteran heavy-hitter,

00:21:04.730 --> 00:21:07.530
Rikiishi was already imagining Leo as Joe.

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:09.350
He was refining

00:21:09.350 --> 00:21:13.960
the timing of his uppercut to use as a weapon in his fight with you.

00:21:14.450 --> 00:21:16.850
And that may not be all.

00:21:16.850 --> 00:21:21.530
I have a feeling he's hiding a more dreadful strategy in that shrunken frame of his.

00:21:21.530 --> 00:21:23.910
An even more dreadful strategy!

00:22:16.130 --> 00:22:18.810
Joe, do you think you have a chance?

00:22:19.410 --> 00:22:20.590
A chance?

00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:25.630
Well, that aside, Rikiishi did well today.

00:22:25.630 --> 00:22:26.820
I was impressed.

00:22:32.070 --> 00:22:34.230
Up until now, I've never gone into a match

00:22:34.230 --> 00:22:36.830
with the slightest thought that I could lose.

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:39.230
I already knew I was going to win.

00:22:39.790 --> 00:22:41.590
But this time is different.

00:22:41.590 --> 00:22:44.340
I don't feel like I can win.

00:22:48.230 --> 00:22:49.120
Shit!

00:22:57.150 --> 00:22:58.150
Joe...

00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:21.580
Rikiishi won after an agonizing battle.

00:23:22.250 --> 00:23:28.310
But Rikiishi's uppercuts were clearly meant to render Joe's Cross Counter useless.

00:23:29.110 --> 00:23:31.130
Although Joe knows this,

00:23:31.130 --> 00:23:35.130
he still claims that the No Guard strategy is the only way to counter the uppercut.

00:23:35.130 --> 00:23:38.570
Together with Nishi and myself,

00:23:38.570 --> 00:23:41.410
he spends day and night coming up with a countermeasure against Rikiishi's uppercuts,

00:23:41.410 --> 00:23:44.560
training in the No Guard Sway Back.

00:23:45.510 --> 00:23:49.570
But, no matter how much training he does,

00:23:49.570 --> 00:23:53.710
the image of Rikiishi, who overcame his endless weight loss, will not leave his mind.

00:23:54.250 --> 00:23:59.810
Now, as Joe seeks to defeat Rikiishi by perfecting the Sway Back,

00:23:59.810 --> 00:24:01.490
which way is tomorrow!?

00:24:16.870 --> 00:24:19.910
Yuke kouya wo

00:24:16.870 --> 00:24:19.910
Go to the wilderness!

00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:23.750
Oira boxer

00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:23.750
I am a boxer.

00:24:24.520 --> 00:24:31.500
Yuuhi ga giragira otoko no yume wa

00:24:24.520 --> 00:24:31.500
The evening sun glitters upon the dreams of men!

00:24:33.220 --> 00:24:37.160
Minna wa kono ore wo nasakemuyo to iu

00:24:33.220 --> 00:24:37.160
Everyone says that I am merciless.

00:24:37.160 --> 00:24:39.200
Tsuki ni hoete hitori

00:24:37.160 --> 00:24:39.200
Howling at the moon alone.

00:24:41.290 --> 00:24:45.420
Oyanashi yadonashi no na mo nai boxer wa

00:24:41.290 --> 00:24:45.420
A parentless, homeless, nameless boxer

00:24:45.420 --> 00:24:48.420
Kusari wo kamikitta Yeah Yeah!

00:24:45.420 --> 00:24:48.420
has bitten off his chains! Yeah, yeah!

00:24:50.150 --> 00:24:53.070
Yuke kouya wo

00:24:50.150 --> 00:24:53.070
Go to the wilderness!

00:24:54.280 --> 00:24:56.780
Oira boxer

00:24:54.280 --> 00:24:56.780
I am a boxer.

00:24:57.890 --> 00:25:05.040
Asahi ga noboru yo otoko no mune ni {removed the Woo, but otherwise japanese is unchanged - Reed}

00:24:57.890 --> 00:25:05.040
The morning sun rises upon the hearts of men!
